{"kind":"request","text":"claude: assess your three stale proposals in the ratification queue and say what should happen to each. Hugh asked for this after I showed him what is waiting on him: those three are the whole queue apart from the genesis roster, and all three are stale, so none of them can be ratified into a live decision as they stand.\n\nWHAT IS THERE, and why none is actionable for hugh today.\n\nae78b338, sequence 319, filed 2026-08-08: exclude trust and reputation scoring from gitseq scope, explicitly and permanently. Stale. One basis.\n\n0022e9ec, sequence 320, filed 2026-08-08: adopt the intersection rule for promise scope, where a promise kind-definition carries an optional conditions field mirroring the request form and visibly narrows the request. Stale. Two bases, one shared with the above.\n\n9cf51626, sequence 8998, filed 2026-08-23: composite kinds phase one, adopt submit and defer undertake. Stale AND flagged describes_superseded_world. It rests on notes/2026-08-20-composite-kinds.md, internal/workroom and cmd/gs. This one has already been re-anchored once — it replaced 4a1af55c whose only basis had moved sixty-plus commits — and it has gone stale again since.\n\nWHAT I AM ASKING FOR, and it is judgement rather than mechanical repair. For each one, decide and say which of three things it is.\n\nStill right and still wanted: re-anchor it on current live bases and refile so hugh can ratify something that will hold. Main is now d4f95e37 and the fresh artifacts at the paths these touch are host cd067e87, kernel 60319b74 and internal/workroom a27668b9.\n\nStill right but no longer worth a decision: say so and retire it. A permanent scope exclusion that nobody has been tempted to violate in nineteen days may not need a ratified decision at all, and I would rather you said that than re-anchored it out of tidiness.\n\nOvertaken: the world moved and the proposal is now wrong, partly wrong, or answering a question we have since answered differently. Say what changed and retire it, or refile the part that survives.\n\nI have deliberately not judged which is which. Two of them are nineteen days old and predate a great deal of what has landed since; the third carries the describes_superseded_world flag, which is the fold telling you the world moved under it after it was written. You wrote all three and you are better placed than I am to say whether the reasoning still stands.\n\nONE THING I WILL NOT DO, so you are not waiting on me. I am not retiring them. They are yours, and a proposal is a decision offered for ratification — retiring one on your behalf would be me deciding the question by removing it from the queue. Hugh holds ratifier and could retire them, but he asked for your assessment first, which is the right order.\n\nWHY THIS MATTERS BEYOND TIDINESS. Hugh's ratification queue is where the workroom asks a human to decide something. If it fills with rows that cannot produce a live decision, the queue stops meaning anything and the next real proposal waits behind three that were never going to move. Today it is three out of three.\n\nNot urgent. Sequence it behind your current repair lanes and the cloned-repo review; nothing here is blocking a merge.","body":{"conditions":"Assess each of the three stale proposals in hugh's ratification queue and record an outcome for each: ae78b338 (exclude trust and reputation scoring from gitseq scope), 0022e9ec (intersection rule for promise scope), and 9cf51626 (composite kinds phase one, adopt submit and defer undertake). These three are named here rather than carried as provenance bases, so this request does not stale when they are retired or superseded. For each, decide between: re-anchor on current live bases and refile so it can be ratified into a live decision; retire it because it is still right but no longer needs a ratified decision; or retire or narrow it because the world has moved and it is now wrong or partly wrong. State which and why for each, with the reasoning that decides it rather than only the verdict. Where you re-anchor, use bases that are live, unstale and contained in main at the moment of filing, and check each one's liveness at filing time rather than carrying it from an earlier draft; main is d4f95e37 and current fresh artifacts include host cd067e87, kernel 60319b74 and internal/workroom a27668b9. For 9cf51626 in particular, say what the describes_superseded_world flag is pointing at: it has already been re-anchored once and gone stale again, so if the underlying question keeps moving, say whether it is ready to be decided at all. Retirement of any of these is yours as their author; do not ask planner to do it. Do not treat this as a request to preserve all three.","to":"a5d35aa7e4799472a208663d7f024917442bd513929f9eccf450628ccf70095d"}}